# 10,000 iterations of random code in ring 3 (tests/programs/fuzz.asm): no
# panic, no reset, no hang, and the kernel's code and tables the same, and
# its GDT's invariants holding, at its checks (test.asm). The kernel prints
# its counts of the fuzz program's faults by vector; that random code ran in
# most of the iterations; and how many the watchdog ended, which must stay
# few. No other thread may fault, or complain on the log: the lines below
# that it must not hold (contains mode passes over any other). The random
# code's own bytes reach the log through KCALL_LOG and PX_WRITE, so the
# summary starts on a line of its own.
program: fuzz
match: contains
timeout: 300
# DOSBox-X stops itself on a far RET through a gate (type 13) (docs/emulators.md).
emulators: bochs mame
forbid: {...} fault #{...}
forbid: {...}cannot go back to its ring{...}
forbid: {...}overflowed its stack{...}
forbid: {...}unhandled IRQ{...}
forbid: {...}the 287 overran a segment{...}
forbid: {...}the 287 reported an error{...}
---
rx286, test build
fuzz: starting
fuzz: faults {...}
fuzz: faults inside the random bytes: {...}, most of the iterations: yes
fuzz: watchdog restarts {...}, {...} of them in a wait on the server; under 5%: yes
fuzz: 10000 iterations; the kernel's code and tables unchanged
